@startuml ViewChildrenListSequence
actor "Teacher" as User
participant "Client UI\n(Classes/index.js)" as UI
participant "Route\nGET /teachers/class" as Route1
participant "Route\nGET /teachers/class/students" as Route2
participant "teacherController" as Controller
participant "Teacher Model" as TeacherModel
participant "User Model" as UserModel
participant "Class Model" as ClassModel
participant "StudentClass Model" as StudentClassModel
participant "Student Model" as StudentModel
database "Database" as DB

== View Classes List ==
User -> UI: Open Classes page
activate UI
UI -> UI: useEffect() triggers
UI -> UI: setLoading(true)
UI -> Route1: GET /teachers/class
activate Route1
Route1 -> Controller: getTeacherClasses(req, res)
activate Controller

Controller -> Controller: getTeacherByReqUser(req)
Controller -> TeacherModel: findOne({ user_id })
activate TeacherModel
TeacherModel -> DB: Query teacher
DB -> TeacherModel: teacher document
TeacherModel -> Controller: teacher
deactivate TeacherModel

Controller -> UserModel: findById(teacher.user_id).select('school_id')
activate UserModel
UserModel -> DB: Query user
DB -> UserModel: user document
UserModel -> Controller: schoolId
deactivate UserModel

Controller -> ClassModel: find({teacher_id or teacher_id2}).populate('school_id', 'class_age_id')
activate ClassModel
ClassModel -> DB: Query classes
DB -> ClassModel: classes array
ClassModel -> Controller: classes
deactivate ClassModel

Controller -> Controller: Group classes by academic_year
Controller -> Controller: Sort by academic_year desc
Controller -> UI: res.json({teacher_id, data: groupedClasses})
deactivate Controller
deactivate Route1

UI -> UI: setGroupedClasses(groups)
UI -> UI: Select latest academic_year
UI -> UI: Select first class of latest year

== View Students List ==
UI -> UI: fetchStudentsForClass(classId)
UI -> Route2: GET /teachers/class/students?class_id=...
activate Route2
Route2 -> Controller: getClassStudents(req, res)
activate Controller

alt class_id not provided
    Controller -> ClassModel: find({teacher_id}).sort({academic_year: -1}).limit(1)
    activate ClassModel
    ClassModel -> DB: Query latest class
    DB -> ClassModel: latest class
    ClassModel -> Controller: latestClass
    deactivate ClassModel
    Controller -> Controller: classId = latestClass._id
end

Controller -> ClassModel: findOne({_id: classId, teacher_id}).populate('school_id', 'class_age_id')
activate ClassModel
ClassModel -> DB: Query class
DB -> ClassModel: class document
ClassModel -> Controller: class
deactivate ClassModel

Controller -> StudentClassModel: find({class_id}).populate('student_id')
activate StudentClassModel
StudentClassModel -> DB: Query student-class mappings
DB -> StudentClassModel: mappings array
StudentClassModel -> Controller: mappings
deactivate StudentClassModel

Controller -> Controller: Map to students array
Controller -> Controller: Build class_info object
Controller -> UI: res.json({class_id, class_info, count, students})
deactivate Controller
deactivate Route2

UI -> UI: setStudents(students)
UI -> UI: setClassInfo(class_info)
UI -> UI: setLoading(false)
UI -> User: Display classes and students list
deactivate UI

@enduml
